.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-disable-tcp-timestamps
command disables TCP timestamps.  This prevents remote attackers
from determining uptime, from which a system's patch level might
be inferred.  Knowing the system patch level helps attackers
determine what kinds of attacks may be effective.

Use with caution: Disabling timestamps may also have negative effects
like reducing network performance and/or stability.  In most cases,
keeping systems up-to-date with all the latest patches is a better
security strategy.  If a system is up-to-date, then knowing its
uptime will only help attackers in the rare case of a known and
recent security regression.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

